// The last will and testament of Margaret Ellis (will.md).
Document "will.md".

Fact person Identified by Margaret, Daniel, Priya, Anna, Ben, Shelter
Role testator Is Margaret
Role residuary Is Shelter
Placeholder witness For person
Placeholder beneficiary For person
Fact asset Identified by House, Cash
Input Fact earlier-will
Param survivorship : Duration = 30

// W.2 Execution: signed, and witnessed by two
Fact witnessed Identified by witness
Bool in-effect
  Holds when Done(sign(Margaret)) && Count(witnessed) >= 2
Act sign Actor testator
  Holds when True
Act attest Actor witness
  Holds when Done(sign(Margaret)) && witness != Margaret
  Creates witnessed(witness)

// W.1 Revocation
Fact revoked Identified by earlier-will
  Holds when in-effect

// W.3 Executor: Daniel, or Priya if Daniel cannot act; authority begins at death
Fact deceased Identified by person
Fact declined Identified by person
Event death Related to person
  Creates deceased(person)
Act decline Actor person
  Holds when True
  Creates declined(person)
Role acting For person First of Daniel, Priya Unless declined(person) || deceased(person)

// W.4 Debts
Input Fact debt Identified by string
Act pay-debt Actor acting Related to string
  Holds when debt(string)
  Terminates debt(string)

// W.5 to W.7 Gifts, survivorship, residue
Fact named Identified by asset * beneficiary
Fact lapsed Identified by beneficiary
  Holds when beneficiary != Margaret
    && (deceased(beneficiary) Before deceased(Margaret)
        || deceased(beneficiary) Within survivorship Of deceased(Margaret))
Fact failed Identified by asset
  Holds when (Exists beneficiary: named(asset, beneficiary) && (lapsed(beneficiary) || witnessed(beneficiary)))
Fact entitled Identified by asset * beneficiary
  Holds when (named(asset, beneficiary) && !failed(asset)) || (residuary(beneficiary) && failed(asset))
Fact received Identified by asset * beneficiary
Act distribute Actor person Recipient beneficiary Related to asset
  Holds when acting(person) && !(Exists debt: debt)
  Valid when in-effect && acting(person) && entitled(asset, beneficiary)
    && Held(deceased(Margaret)) For survivorship
  Creates received(asset, beneficiary)

Clause W.1 Definition => revoked
Clause W.2/1 => sign, attest, in-effect
Clause W.2/2 => failed, distribute
Clause W.3/1 => acting, decline
Clause W.3/2 => distribute
Clause W.4 => pay-debt, distribute
Clause W.5 => named(House, Anna), named(Cash, Ben)
Clause W.6 => survivorship, lapsed, failed
Clause W.7 => residuary, entitled, distribute.
